# Agent & Frontend Integration Guide: `django-social-autoposter` (v0.3.0)

A standalone Django REST Framework package for broadcasting social media posts at once to Facebook, Instagram, Threads, TikTok, X (Twitter), LinkedIn, and sending direct private messages across WhatsApp, Instagram, Facebook Messenger, X, and LinkedIn.

---

## 🔒 Authentication
All endpoints require DRF token authentication:
```http
Authorization: Token <user_token>
# OR
Authorization: Bearer <jwt_access_token>
```

---

## 📡 REST API Endpoints

### 1. Broadcast Post to All / Selected Platforms
* **Endpoint:** `POST /social/broadcast/`
* **Request Payload:**
```json
{
  "title": "Exciting Announcement",
  "message": "We have just released our new platform features! Check it out now.",
  "link_url": "https://example.com/announcement",
  "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/image/upload/sample.jpg",
  "platforms": ["facebook", "instagram", "threads", "tiktok", "twitter", "linkedin"]
}
```
> **Tip:** You can omit the `"platforms"` array or pass `null` to automatically post to all platforms currently enabled in `.env` or the database.

* **Response (HTTP 201 Created):**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Exciting Announcement",
  "message": "We have just released our new platform features! Check it out now.",
  "link_url": "https://example.com/announcement",
  "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/image/upload/sample.jpg",
  "target_platforms": ["facebook", "twitter", "linkedin", "instagram"],
  "content_type": null,
  "object_id": null,
  "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:30:00Z",
  "logs": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "broadcast": 1,
      "platform": "facebook",
      "status": "published",
      "external_post_id": "109876543210_12345",
      "external_post_url": "https://facebook.com/109876543210_12345",
      "error_message": null,
      "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:30:02Z"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "broadcast": 1,
      "platform": "twitter",
      "status": "published",
      "external_post_id": "1840000000000000000",
      "external_post_url": "https://x.com/i/web/status/1840000000000000000",
      "error_message": null,
      "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:30:02Z"
    }
  ]
}
```

### 2. View Broadcast History
* **Endpoint:** `GET /social/broadcast/`
* Returns all past broadcasts with nested status logs.

### 3. Filter Execution Logs
* **Endpoint:** `GET /social/logs/?platform=facebook&status=failed`
* Filters audit logs by platform (`facebook`, `instagram`, `twitter`, `linkedin`) or status (`published`, `failed`, `pending`, `skipped`).

### 4. Twitter / X OAuth 1.0a User Context Requirements
Twitter's `POST /2/tweets` endpoint requires **OAuth 1.0a User Context** tokens (or OAuth 2.0 User Context). Bearer Tokens (App-Only) are rejected with 403 Forbidden.
Required tokens in `.env` or `SocialPlatformConfig`:
- `TWITTER_API_KEY`: Consumer Key
- `TWITTER_API_SECRET`: Consumer Secret
- `TWITTER_ACCESS_TOKEN`: User Access Token
- `TWITTER_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET`: User Access Token Secret

⚠️ **Developer Portal Permission Warning**: In [developer.x.com](https://developer.x.com/) under Project & App settings -> **User authentication settings**, permissions must be set to **"Read and write"** before generating/regenerating the tokens.

---

## 💬 Direct Messaging Endpoints

### 5. Send Direct Message (WhatsApp, Instagram, FB Messenger, X, LinkedIn)
* **Endpoint:** `POST /social/messages/send/`
* **Request Payload:**
```json
{
  "platform": "whatsapp",
  "recipient_id": "+15551234567",
  "message": "Hello! Your appointment is confirmed for tomorrow at 10:00 AM.",
  "media_url": "https://example.com/confirmation.pdf",
  "extra_params": {
    "media_type": "document",
    "filename": "confirmation.pdf"
  }
}
```
* **Supported `platform` Values:**
  * `"whatsapp"`: `recipient_id` is phone number (E.164 digits). Supports `extra_params`: `media_type` (`image`, `document`, `video`, `audio`), `template`.
  * `"instagram"`: `recipient_id` is Instagram Scoped User ID (IGSID).
  * `"facebook"`: `recipient_id` is Page-scoped User ID (PSID). Supports `extra_params`: `tag` (`ACCOUNT_UPDATE`, `CONFIRMED_EVENT_UPDATE`, `POST_PURCHASE_UPDATE`).
  * `"twitter"`: `recipient_id` is X User ID (digits).
  * `"linkedin"`: `recipient_id` is member ID (or `urn:li:person:...`).

* **Response (HTTP 201 Created on delivery):**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "platform": "whatsapp",
  "recipient_id": "+15551234567",
  "sender_id": null,
  "message": "Hello! Your appointment is confirmed for tomorrow at 10:00 AM.",
  "media_url": "https://example.com/confirmation.pdf",
  "direction": "outbound",
  "status": "delivered",
  "external_message_id": "wamid.HBgL...",
  "conversation_id": null,
  "error_message": null,
  "response_data": {
    "messages": [{"id": "wamid.HBgL..."}]
  },
  "extra_data": {
    "media_type": "document"
  },
  "created_at": "2026-11-15T16:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-11-15T16:00:01Z"
}
```

### 6. List Direct Messages
* **Endpoint:** `GET /social/messages/`
* **Query Params:**
  * `?platform=whatsapp`
  * `?recipient_id=+15551234567`
  * `?status=delivered`
  * `?direction=outbound`

### 7. Retrieve Message Details
* **Endpoint:** `GET /social/messages/<id>/`
* **Delete Message Log:** `DELETE /social/messages/<id>/`
